Fixed all three findings:

- `declare_replacing_binding` now also updates the current block scope, so a `set` shadows a function declared in the same branch body.
- `scope_function_binding` now requires the function declaration to precede the use, preventing forward jumps past a shadowing `set`.
- Added `edge_set_shadows_a_function_declared_in_the_same_branch` and `edge_call_after_a_set_does_not_reach_a_later_function`.
